{
  "id": "a2-u08-l03",
  "unit": "a2-u08",
  "order": 3,
  "title": "As well as you",
  "goal": "Say as … as and like with kadar and gibi, say how much with pek, oldukça and biraz, and use adjectives as adverbs: Senin kadar iyi konuşamıyorum.",
  "points": ["gp-equative", "gp-adjectives-as-adverbs"],
  "intro": {
    "text": "*Kadar* means **as … as**, *gibi* means **like**: *Can kadar uzun* (as tall as Can), *bir kardeş gibi* (like a brother). After *ben, sen, o, biz, siz*, use the genitive: *benim kadar*, *senin gibi*. And an adjective before a verb is an adverb: *iyi konuşuyor* (she speaks well).",
    "see": "gp-equative"
  },
  "vocab": [
    {
      "tr": "kadar",
      "en": "as … as; as much as (after a dative: until)",
      "pos": "postp",
      "card": "fc-0036"
    },
    {
      "tr": "gibi",
      "en": "like, as",
      "pos": "postp",
      "card": "fc-0037"
    },
    {
      "tr": "pek",
      "en": "very; not very (with a negative)",
      "pos": "adv",
      "card": "fc-0254"
    },
    {
      "tr": "oldukça",
      "en": "quite, fairly",
      "pos": "adv",
      "card": "fc-0415"
    },
    {
      "tr": "benzemek",
      "en": "to look like, to resemble",
      "pos": "verb",
      "card": "fc-0356"
    },
    {
      "tr": "dikkatli",
      "en": "careful; carefully",
      "pos": "adj",
      "card": "fc-0591"
    },
    {
      "tr": "rahat",
      "en": "comfortable; at ease",
      "pos": "adj",
      "card": "fc-0430"
    }
  ],
